    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1505">

                <pb facs="1215" n="1099" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1099"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/427.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 17.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 7, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith three
                    copies of the Official Gazette, dated March 30, 1912, containing Spanish text of
                    the <pb facs="1216" n="1100" xml:id="pg1100"/> new currency law<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1505-f1"/> enacted by the National Assembly of Nicaragua on March
                    20, 1912, as reported in my telegram of that date. I am also transmitting a copy
                    of a letter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1505-f2"/> addressed to me by Mr. Conant, the
                    currency expert, with its enclosure of the English text of said law as prepared
                    by the bankers who have the loan and monetary matters in charge.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George T. Weitzel.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
